Name:           grok-bot-linux
Version:        @VERSION@
Release:        1%{?dist}
Summary:        Helper that installs Cursor's official Grok Bot on Linux
License:        MIT
URL:            https://github.com/devrecated/grok-bot-linux
BuildArch:      noarch
Requires:       curl python3 ca-certificates coreutils
Recommends:     gnupg2

%description
Ships the MIT-licensed install scripts from grok-bot-linux. Run
grok-bot-linux-setup after installing to download and verify Cursor's
official .deb, .rpm, or AppImage. The package never redistributes
xAI or Cursor binaries.

This is an unofficial community project and is not affiliated with xAI
or Cursor.

%prep

%install
rm -rf %{buildroot}
mkdir -p %{buildroot}
cp -a %{stagedir}/. %{buildroot}/

%files
/usr/lib/grok-bot-linux
/usr/bin/grok-bot-linux-setup
/usr/share/doc/grok-bot-linux

%post
cat <<'MSG'
grok-bot-linux: helper scripts installed.

This package does not contain Grok Bot. To download and verify Cursor's
official Linux build, run:

  sudo grok-bot-linux-setup

Or, for a specific format: sudo grok-bot-linux-setup --format appimage
MSG

%changelog
* Tue Oct 20 2026 Adam Siwiec <73085927+adamsiwiec1@users.noreply.github.com> - @VERSION@-1
- Initial helper package (scripts only; official build fetched at setup time)
